A||||7||My7Fieros||Do I need an adapter to add a GT steering wheel to a non-GT car?||||5||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||11-26-2001||09:15 PM||||Im going to get a new leather GT steering wheel from the Fiero Store to put in my 86 SE. It has the regular 4 spoker w/ the horn paddles in it now. I thought I read somewhere that you need some kind of an adapter. Is this true? If so, what is it I need? Also didnt somebody say something about plastic rivets that need to be reworked or something on the Fiero Store steering wheels? TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||11-26-2001||09:45 PM||||I think all stock steering wheels are interchangeable. However, if you get the fierostore GT wheel, you'll need the hub from a GT wheel. I've also heard they're a bit smaller than the stock wheels.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||11-26-2001||09:47 PM||||Not sure about the FS wheels but I just put an 84 wheel on my GT (old story melted mush and two(2) wheel covers).  No problem.<P>I have a wood rim Grant wheel on my SE and yes you do need an adapter for them.<P>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||11-27-2001||02:28 AM||||*||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||11-27-2001||02:52 AM||||I am doing the same swap with my formula.  The steering wheel is driving me nuts.  I e-mailed the fiero store and this is what they said:<P>You will need the horn assembly, including &gt;it's wiring and the plastic trim<BR>&gt;piece that fits around the hub (between the &gt;column and wheel). You can use<BR>&gt;the trim/horn pieces from a 3 spoke GT or &gt;SE wheel.<P><BR>Mrfiero is looking into getting me the parts that are needed.  I searched and found one forum member who has done the swap with the FS GT wheel.  He has not responded to my e-mails, but from what I can tell the plastic hub is riveted on.  You will need to screw that part on to the new FS wheel. I will let you know how mine goes!!<P>Ross<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSoul||11-27-2001||06:37 AM||||  I changed mine a month or so back. I didn't have the right size rivets to reattach the horn button to the wheel and collar so as a temporary thing I simply snapped them back together. (The horn button has snap clips that go through the wheel and grasp the collar) After I installed it I could find no reason to get the rivets!  Still works and I have had no problems!||||reg||6
Z||000006||K2m4||11-29-2001||11:37 AM||||PLUG and PLAY...I have an 88 gt steering wheel in my 86 2m4...fits like a glove<P><BR>Kerm <BR>86 GT<BR>86 2M4<BR>||||reg||1
